  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-4000004714</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mitigating Local Conflict and Supporting Community Protection Systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Nonviolent Peaceforce (NP) proposal is based on two parallel objectives: 1). Mitigate acute risks of violence against civilians through middle of direct protection and prevention, and 2). Promote responsiveness and effectiveness of security carriers to protect civilians. The activity takes place in Sinjar and Ba&apos;aj, Ninewa, where tensions between different groups and between the community and security authorities are high. Ninewa is thereby the province where most of Iraq&apos;s still 1.3 internally displaced people both live and come from. NP&apos;s work responds to a crucial gap in traditional local security activities, by focusing on the security demands of the different gropes in the area and working from there to improve relations between the community and security authorities. NP works according to their self-developed and scientifically accepted Unarmed Civilian Protection (UCP) methodology and the staff is permanently present in the area for the duration of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
